Subject: Zero-initialize the Broadcom default WoWLAN configuration

The driver initializes just four default trigger booleans. With ordinary
MALLOC, cfg80211 can report unrelated wake triggers, including any, from
whatever bytes were already in the other fields. Zero the allocation and
retain the explicit defaults and user-configured overrides.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd4361/wl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd4361/wl_cfg80211.c
@@ -12580,7 +12580,7 @@
 	/* If this is not provided cfg stack will get disconnect
 	* during suspend.
 	*/
-	brcm_wowlan_config = MALLOC(dhd->osh, sizeof(struct cfg80211_wowlan));
+	brcm_wowlan_config = MALLOCZ(dhd->osh, sizeof(struct cfg80211_wowlan));
 	if (brcm_wowlan_config) {
 		brcm_wowlan_config->disconnect = true;
 		brcm_wowlan_config->gtk_rekey_failure = true;
